  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A tennis ball is travelling horizontally at speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>, hits a vertical wall and rebounds. The ball loses <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> % of its initial energy during the collision. The mass of the ball is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span>. The magnitude of the impulse by the wall on the ball is:</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left (1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}  \\right )mv\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left (1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}  \\right )mv\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}mv\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3}{2}mv\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
